ders try to stay alive on a sneaky-good Week 12 slate.","published":"2026-11-20T16:00:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532397/connelly-week-12-preview-big-ten-tennessee","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State's club team might be the Buckeyes' most dominant program","description":"One football team in Columbus still has national title hopes. Just not the one with Jeremiah Smith.","published":"2026-11-20T16:21:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522496/ohio-state-club-football","type":"Story","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"'Another universe': How Indiana football changed Bloomington","description":"The basketball haven has become a legend of the fall, where the reigning national champs take center stage.","published":"2026-11-20T16:31:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50533477/bloomington-indiana-football-town","type":"Story","byline":"Chuck Culpepper","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"SEC standardized NIL, revenue sharing contracts 'unfair' for players, agents say","description":"The SEC's new uniform NIL and revenue sharing agreements are causing an uproar among agents concerned that the contracts are loaded with terms that are unfair.","published":"2026-11-20T01:16:03.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50535591/sec-standardized-nil-contracts-unfair-players-agents-say","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Waiver approved allowing Army, Navy to play 13th game in 2027","description":"The waiver will allow Army and Navy to play 12 games apiece before the College Football Playoff selections are made and keep their rivalry game.","published":"2026-11-20T14:06:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50535192/waiver-approved-army-navy-13th-game-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"James Madison moving to American Conference in 2027","description":"James Madison is leaving the Sun Belt Conference for the American Conference a year earlier than planned, in 2027 rather than 2028.","published":"2026-11-19T21:30:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50534149/james-madison-moving-american-conference-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5082149/clev-lubin","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clev_Lubin"},"pick":{"pick":56,"round":2,"team":"ATL","via":"JAX","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Clev Lubin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clev_Lubin","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:13Z","intro":"Clevmer Lubin (CLEV-mah LOO-bin) is an American college football defensive end for the Louisville Cardinals. He previously played for the Army Black Knights, Iowa Western Reivers, and Coastal Carolina Chanticleers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Lubin played football and basketball for Suffern High School and was considered one of the best players the school has produced. He played as both a defensive end and running back, and during his senior season he recorded 1,053 rushing yards and 16 touchdowns on 110 carries. He also set a program record of 1,062 rushing yards during the 2019 season. Due to his success on the field, he was named the Gatorade New York State Player of the Year as a senior and was also named The Journal News Rockland County Football Player of the Year. Lubin received several Division I offers, and on December 14, 2020, he committed to play at Army. Following his senior season, Lubin spent a year prepping at USMAPS before joining the Black Knights in 2022."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"ARMY\nAfter joining the Black Knights, Lubin did not see any game action his true freshman season and transferred to Iowa Western.\n\nIOWA WESTERN\nWhile at Iowa Western, Lubin helped lead the team to the NJCAA D1 Football National Championship. Following the season he was named a first-team NJCAA All-American.\n\nCOASTAL CAROLINA\nOn July 1, 2024, Lubin enrolled at Coastal Carolina. In 10 games, he finished 16th nationally in sacks and contributed 12.5 tackles for loss. Following the season, he was given First-Team All-Sun Belt honors.\nAfter the season, Lubin again entered the transfer portal.\n\nLOUISVILLE\nOn December 21, 2024, Lubin committed to Louisville. On January 2, 2026, Lubin announced he would return to Louisville for another season."}]}}